{
  "title": "Burn down Ruff import-order and module-name ignores",
  "description": "To get root-level Ruff lint passing without churning unrelated files, `ruff-lint.toml` currently suppresses `I001` in several scripts and `N999` for hyphenated script module names under `scripts/*-*.py`.\n\
\n\
There are two separate cleanup tracks here:\n\
- fix import ordering in the files that still carry `I001`\n\
- decide whether hyphenated script filenames should stay and keep the `N999` suppression, or be renamed to lint-clean module names with CLI wrappers if needed\n\
\n\
Relevant files:\n\
- `ruff-lint.toml`\n\
- `scripts/analysis/blunder_analysis.py`\n\
- `scripts/analysis/blunder_eval.py`\n\
- `scripts/analysis/blunder_eval_common.py`\n\
- `scripts/analysis/extract_decisions.py`\n\
- `scripts/claim-issue.py`\n\
- `scripts/export_game.py`\n\
- `scripts/*-*.py`",
